! Rendered by the interop suite from an frrConfig; see frr.go.
!
! Deliberate stances baked in rather than rediscovered per scenario:
! - isis network point-to-point on the harness interface. RFC 5309
!   requires both ends to agree and a mismatch is silent by design, so
!   the one circuit type this library implements is always set.
! - Short hello timers, so a holding time costs seconds rather than the
!   ISO default's half minute.
! - No topology ipv6-unicast. This library is single topology, and
!   multi-topology negotiation is not a precondition for an adjacency.
! - Hello padding left at FRR's default of always, so every scenario
!   receives the interface-MTU hellos which a receive buffer sized to
!   ISO's 1492 would silently truncate.
! - debug isis adj-packets and events, so a failure has a transcript.
frr defaults traditional
hostname frr-interop
log stdout
debug isis adj-packets
debug isis events
!
interface {{.Interface}}
 ip router isis lab
 ipv6 router isis lab
 isis network point-to-point
 isis circuit-type level-2
 isis hello-interval {{.HelloInterval}}
 isis hello-multiplier {{.HelloMultiplier}}
exit
!
router isis lab
 net {{.NET}}
 is-type level-2-only
 metric-style wide
 hostname dynamic
exit
